WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.345
Male veterans: one point four times the civilian suicide rate.

00:00:04.295 --> 00:00:07.557
Female veterans: one point nine times.

00:00:07.557 --> 00:00:12.715
Forty-two years of elevated suicide risk documented with zero meaningful improvement.

00:00:12.715 --> 00:00:17.488
Three thousand to five thousand Canadian veterans are homeless on any given night.

00:00:17.488 --> 00:00:23.068
Forty-seven percent of disability applications now miss the sixteen-week processing standard.

00:00:23.068 --> 00:00:27.670
The backlog doubled — from five thousand six hundred to over eleven thousand.

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:30.931
Twenty-four percent of mental health claims denied.

00:00:30.931 --> 00:00:34.511
One in four veterans told their suffering does not qualify.

00:00:34.511 --> 00:00:38.102
A wheelchair ramp costs three to eight thousand dollars.

00:00:38.102 --> 00:00:40.715
MAID costs twenty-five hundred.

00:00:40.715 --> 00:00:44.056
It is cheaper to kill a veteran than to install a ramp.

00:00:44.056 --> 00:00:50.045
Four to five confirmed cases of Veterans Affairs employees offering MAID to veterans who called asking for help.

00:00:50.045 --> 00:00:52.147
They called for a wheelchair.

00:00:52.147 --> 00:00:54.102
They were offered death.
